    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response following standard Spring/MapStruct conventions used throughout this codebase for the other derived presentation fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time), documented as `'SILVER'` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `'BRONZE'`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added an `@AfterMapping` hook `addMembershipTier` that sets the tier: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** a non-empty email is present, else `BRONZE` (with null-safety mirroring the sibling mappers).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass \u2014 `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique owner + email \u2192 SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 BRONZE).",
